${macro.generated_by(self.path)}

=[ Common Files ]

The files that the repositories of the Tomet ecosystem share, kept once. A repository takes the ones it needs with @link[ catasto ](target: "https://github.com/tomet-lang/fs-catasto"), which pins each to a commit and a SHA-256, and `catasto check` (run by `sisho check`) says when a copy has been edited or has drifted.

Like `dotfiles`, the name is a convention: a repository of the common files of one person or one organisation, to be taken the same way.

==[ What is here ]

-| `LICENSE-APACHE`, `LICENSE-MIT` -- the license texts the repositories carry.
-| `.editorconfig` -- the editor settings.
-| `nix/formatter.nix` -- the `treefmt` setup the flakes use for `nix fmt`.

==[ Taking a file ]

```bash
catasto upstream add commonfiles https://github.com/tomet-lang/commonfiles.git
catasto add LICENSE-MIT --upstream commonfiles LICENSE-MIT
catasto add .editorconfig --upstream commonfiles .editorconfig
catasto add nix/formatter.nix --upstream commonfiles nix/formatter.nix
```

That declares the files in `catasto.ctmt`, copies them and writes `catasto.lock`. Commit the three. To take a newer version of one file later:

```bash
catasto sync --update --only LICENSE-MIT
```

A file here is never edited in the repository that took it: change it here, then take it again.

==[ Adding a file ]

Only a file that is the same in every repository that has it belongs here. A file that differs by a name or a list (`.gitignore`, `default.config.tmt`) stays where it is.
